{"title":"1961 AHSME Problems/Problem 3","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>If the graphs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/7/f47f69f05b4e5821e677b97fe3343e9b4f64ec64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y+x+3=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"115\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/e/7de93ff8c551106b26ae806a200de169cc74d655.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y+ax+2=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"125\" height=\"16\" /> are to meet at right angles, the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/3/fa31a02950a9fcb9324059ca103ceef5a027b538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\pm \\frac{2}{3} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ -\\frac{3}{2} \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 6\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ -6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"449\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The slope of the first graph is -1/2. The slope of the second is 2, since it is perpendicular, and it is also -a/3 by rearranging. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0aff89088d84219bd199f1fe8fac356f57fd7010.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=-6$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" />.  Answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><i>By Ajeet Dubey | <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://ioqm.in\">ioqm.in</a></i>\n</p><p><b>Step 1: Determine the two slopes.</b>\n</p><p>Writing the lines in slope-intercept form gives slopes\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2be30daa4665476407b86395fd748000831c05d4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1=-\\frac12\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad m_2=-\\frac a3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"250\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><b>Step 2: Use perpendicularity.</b>\n</p><p>Perpendicular nonvertical lines satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c48b18d3b71717bc10211cf23f8d5c957f93a661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_1m_2=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Thus\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/0/c1059c10520299625e28c9af290a7eab52012c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left(-\\frac12\\right)\\left(-\\frac a3\\right)=-1, \\qquad \\frac a6=-1, \\qquad a=-6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"360\" height=\"45\" />\n</p><p>Thus the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/f/6bfc0829f3f29bbf35d0a861644e00cfef0f50ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"39\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME\" title=\"1961 AHSME\">1961 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1961 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1961_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1961 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1961\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Pre